

# TV Gamer Buying Checklist 2026

Technical checklist for evaluating televisions for PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X.

This guide is intended to help compare specifications according to actual use rather than simply selecting the model with the largest numbers.

## 1. Console requirements

For current-generation console gaming, check:

- [x] 4K
- [ ] 120 Hz
- [ ] VRR
- [ ] HDMI capability
- [ ] Low-latency/game mode
- [ ] HDR

## 2. Refresh rate

Do not assume that 165 Hz automatically provides an advantage over 120 Hz on a console.

PS5 and Xbox Series X support compatible gaming modes up to 120 Hz.

Higher refresh rates can become more useful when the same display is connected to a compatible PC.

## 3. Panel technology

### OLED

Consider when:

- dark-room gaming is common;
- deep blacks are a priority;
- high contrast is important;
- cinematic games and movies are part of the use case.

### Mini LED

Consider when:

- the room is bright;
- high brightness is important;
- gaming, movies and sports will share the display.

Neither technology should be treated as universally superior.

## 4. HDMI checklist

Verify the exact ports rather than relying only on the model's general specification.

Check:

- 4K/120 Hz support;
- VRR;
- required bandwidth;
- number of high-capability ports.

## 5. Multiple-device setup

Example:

```text
PS5
Xbox Series X
Gaming PC
Soundbar
```

In this scenario, HDMI capacity can become an important part of the buying decision.

## 6. Room conditions

### Bright room

Prioritize:

- brightness;
- reflection behavior;
- screen positioning.

### Dark room

Prioritize:

- contrast;
- black levels;
- panel behavior in dark scenes.

## 7. Previous-generation models

Do not automatically discard an older generation.

Compare:

```text
Price difference
        +
Actual feature difference
        +
Intended usage
```

A previous-generation model can remain relevant when it retains the features that matter to the intended use and is significantly cheaper.

